{"type":"message","id":"d606bb6f","parentId":"867527a1","timestamp":"2026-04-23T11:04:23.972Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_RYvl6Oq3DbDugqeIJkO473qE|fc_0e8434613da66f1e0169e9fca9968881919ac59f83421f52aa","toolName":"process","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"domain\": [\n    \"nephrology\",\n    \"hypertension\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"Signs such as elevated blood pressure levels leading to grade 2 or grade 3 hypertension, increased risk factors like diabetes mellitus, decreased albumin-to-creatinine ratio indicating worsening renal impairment, and persistent high serum creatinine values may indicate kidney damage that requires monitoring in hypertensive individuals.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"./data/nephrology/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf\",\n    \"./data/hypertension/2023 ESH Guidelines for the management of arterial hypertens... _ Journal of Hypertension.pdf\"\n  ],\n  \"retrieved_chunks\": [\n    \"Stricter BP targets, i.e. below the 75th percentile or below the 50th percentile for 24 h mean BP, are recommended for CKD either with [925,937,938] or without proteinuria, respectively . Treatment should start with lifestyle changes, within which loss of body weight has a primary importance because of the close association of [925,939,940] hypertension and obesity in adolescents . The decision to use antihypertensive drugs should be based on failure to reach BP control and also, concomitantly with lifestyle interventions, on the BP level (grade 2 or 3 hypertension), the presence of signs or symptoms related to the BP elevation and the evidence of HMOD. Drug treatment should be implemented according to a step care approach. The same five major drug classes validated in adult [925,939,940] hypertensive patients are recommended . 15.1.3 Transition period to adulthood\",\n    \"risk, and change of albuminuria was related to total mortality, CV events and kidney outcomes [294] in both diabetic and nondiabetic patients . That is, patients with a decrease of albuminuria by 50% had a lower mortality, while an increase of albuminuria by 100% was associated with adverse CV and kidney outcome as well as a higher mortality. BP reduction by antihypertensive treatment often leads to an acute increase (up to 20–30%) in serum creatinine, especially if treatment makes use of RAS-blockers. This is interpreted as having a hemodynamic basis (BP- dependent reduction of GFR) and, thus, not to usually reflect kidney injury. However, the long- term clinical significance of this early treatment-associated reduction of kidney function is still [295,296] unclear . Serum creatinine, eGFR and ACR should be documented in all hypertensive [290] patients, and if CKD is diagnosed, repeated at least annually . One negative urinary dipstick [297]\",\n    \"Adv Chronic Kidney Dis. 2018;25: Nephrol.2011;33:121–130. 67–75. 165. Rosner MH, Jhaveri KD, Mc Mahon BA, et al. Onconephrology: the 189. PotokOA,RifkinDE,IxJH,etal.EstimatedGFRaccuracywhencystatinC- intersections between the kidney and cancer. CA Cancer J Clin. and creatinine-based estimates are discrepant in older adults. Kidney 2021;71:47–77. Med.2023;5:100628. 166. SoveriI,BergUB,BjorkJ,etal.MeasuringGFR:asystematicreview.AmJ 190. FarringtonDK,SurapaneniA,MatsushitaK,etal.Discrepanciesbetween Kidney Dis.2014;64:411–424. cystatin C-based and creatinine-based eGFR. Clin J Am Soc Nephrol. 167. WhiteCA,AkbariA,AllenC,etal.Simultaneousglomerularfiltrationrate 2023;18:1143–1152. determinationusinginulin,iohexol,and99m Tc-DTPAdemonstratesthe 191. CoreshJ,TotoRD,KirkKA,etal.Creatinineclearanceasameasureof needforcustomizedmeasurementprotocols. Kidney Int.2021;99:957– GFR in screenees for the African-American study of kidney disease 966. andhypertensionpilotstudy.AmJKidney Dis.1998;32:32–42. 168. Xie P, Huang JM, LiuXM, etal. (99m)Tc-DTPA renal dynamic imaging 192. Krupka E, Curtis S, Ferguson T, et al. The effect of gender-affirming method may be unsuitable to be used as the reference method in hormonetherapyonmeasuresofkidneyfunction:asystematicreview investigating the validity of CDK-EPI equation for determining andmeta-analysis.ClinJAm Soc Nephrol.2022;17:1305–1315. glomerularfiltrationrate.PLoSOne.2013;8:e62328. 193. van Eeghen SA, Wiepjes CM, T’Sjoen G, et al. Cystatin C-based eGFR 169.\",\n    \"associated with mortality across stages of chronic kidney disease: the 539. Adamczak M, Surma S. Metabolic acidosis in patients with CKD: Stockholm CREAtinine Measurements (SCREAM) project. Nephrol Dial epidemiology, pathogenesis, and treatment.Kidney Dis(Basel).2021;7: Transplant.2019;34:1534–1541. 452–467. 562. GoyalA,SpertusJA,GoschK,etal.Serumpotassiumlevelsandmortality 540. MelamedML,RaphaelKL.MetabolicacidosisinCKD:areviewofrecent inacutemyocardialinfarction.JAMA.2012;307:157–164. findings.Kidney Med.2021;3:267–277. 563. KolasaKM.Dietary Approachesto Stop Hypertension(DASH)inclinical 541. InkerLA,GramsME,LeveyAS,etal.RelationshipofestimatedGFRand practice:aprimarycareexperience.Clin Cardiol.1999;22:III16–III22. albuminuria to concurrent laboratory abnormalities: an individual 564. Nakhoul GN, Huang H, Arrigain S, et al. Serum potassium, end-stage participantdatameta-analysisina Global Consortium.AmJKidney Dis. renal disease and mortality in chronic kidney disease. Am J Nephrol. 2019;73:206–217. 2015;41:456–463. 542. Hultin S, Hood C, Campbell KL, et al. A systematic review and meta- 565. AllonM,ShanklinN.Effectofalbuteroltreatmentonsubsequentdialytic analysisoneffectsofbicarbonatetherapyonkidneyoutcomes.Kidney potassiumremoval.AmJKidney Dis.1995;26:607–613. Int Rep.2021;6:695–705. 566. FosterES,JonesWJ,HayslettJP,etal.Roleofaldosteroneanddietary 543. Bi Carb Study Group. Clinical and cost-effectiveness of oral sodium potassium in potassium adaptation in the distal colon of the rat. bicarbonate therapy for older patients with chronic kidney disease Gastroenterology.1985;88:41–46.\"\n  ]\n}\n\nProcess exited with code 0."}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"vivid-valley","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"{\n  \"domain\": [\n    \"nephrology\",\n    \"hypertension\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"Signs such as elevated blood pressure levels leading to grade 2 or grade 3 hypertension, increased risk factors like diabetes mellitus, decreased albumin-to-creatinine ratio indicating worsening renal impairment, and persistent high serum creatinine values may indicate kidney damage that requires monitoring in hypertensive individuals.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"./data/nephrology/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf\",\n    \"./data/hypertension/2023 ESH Guidelines for the management of arterial hypertens... _ Journal of Hypertension.pdf\"\n  ],\n  \"retrieved_chunks\": [\n    \"Stricter BP targets, i.e. below the 75th percentile or below the 50th percentile for 24 h mean BP, are recommended for CKD either with [925,937,938] or without proteinuria, respectively . Treatment should start with lifestyle changes, within which loss of body weight has a primary importance because of the close association of [925,939,940] hypertension and obesity in adolescents . The decision to use antihypertensive drugs should be based on failure to reach BP control and also, concomitantly with lifestyle interventions, on the BP level (grade 2 or 3 hypertension), the presence of signs or symptoms related to the BP elevation and the evidence of HMOD. Drug treatment should be implemented according to a step care approach. The same five major drug classes validated in adult [925,939,940] hypertensive patients are recommended . 15.1.3 Transition period to adulthood\",\n    \"risk, and change of albuminuria was related to total mortality, CV events and kidney outcomes [294] in both diabetic and nondiabetic patients . That is, patients with a decrease of albuminuria by 50% had a lower mortality, while an increase of albuminuria by 100% was associated with adverse CV and kidney outcome as well as a higher mortality. BP reduction by antihypertensive treatment often leads to an acute increase (up to 20–30%) in serum creatinine, especially if treatment makes use of RAS-blockers. This is interpreted as having a hemodynamic basis (BP- dependent reduction of GFR) and, thus, not to usually reflect kidney injury. However, the long- term clinical significance of this early treatment-associated reduction of kidney function is still [295,296] unclear . Serum creatinine, eGFR and ACR should be documented in all hypertensive [290] patients, and if CKD is diagnosed, repeated at least annually . One negative urinary dipstick [297]\",\n    \"Adv Chronic Kidney Dis. 2018;25: Nephrol.2011;33:121–130. 67–75. 165. Rosner MH, Jhaveri KD, Mc Mahon BA, et al. Onconephrology: the 189. PotokOA,RifkinDE,IxJH,etal.EstimatedGFRaccuracywhencystatinC- intersections between the kidney and cancer. CA Cancer J Clin. and creatinine-based estimates are discrepant in older adults. Kidney 2021;71:47–77. Med.2023;5:100628. 166. SoveriI,BergUB,BjorkJ,etal.MeasuringGFR:asystematicreview.AmJ 190. FarringtonDK,SurapaneniA,MatsushitaK,etal.Discrepanciesbetween Kidney Dis.2014;64:411–424. cystatin C-based and creatinine-based eGFR. Clin J Am Soc Nephrol. 167. WhiteCA,AkbariA,AllenC,etal.Simultaneousglomerularfiltrationrate 2023;18:1143–1152. determinationusinginulin,iohexol,and99m Tc-DTPAdemonstratesthe 191. CoreshJ,TotoRD,KirkKA,etal.Creatinineclearanceasameasureof needforcustomizedmeasurementprotocols. Kidney Int.2021;99:957– GFR in screenees for the African-American study of kidney disease 966. andhypertensionpilotstudy.AmJKidney Dis.1998;32:32–42. 168. Xie P, Huang JM, LiuXM, etal. (99m)Tc-DTPA renal dynamic imaging 192. Krupka E, Curtis S, Ferguson T, et al. The effect of gender-affirming method may be unsuitable to be used as the reference method in hormonetherapyonmeasuresofkidneyfunction:asystematicreview investigating the validity of CDK-EPI equation for determining andmeta-analysis.ClinJAm Soc Nephrol.2022;17:1305–1315. glomerularfiltrationrate.PLoS